                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6aa69f77-e4c4-4115-86c7-13ebb94a1b20",
                        "source_entry_id": "0d6d64b8-fac1-34b2-908b-4c1639fd54e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "d50245d2-6b17-3906-8214-f31e83c59cc4",
                        "target_lang_word": "anti-tank",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anti-tank",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7dc1d764-45b7-3faf-8d60-6b2264a58bc1",
                                        "entry_id": "dcf73b60-6a76-3fc5-aa2f-a0b8af916193",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of antitank."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40c1e30e-f247-4549-a942-202d069ca1d5",
                                                "sense_id": "7dc1d764-45b7-3faf-8d60-6b2264a58bc1",
                                                "text": "\"For the first time in 125 years a powerful enemy was now established across the narrow waters of the English Channel. ... Many people must have been bewildered by the innumerable activities all around them. They could understand the necessity for wiring and mining the beaches, the anti-tank obstacles at the defiles, the concrete pillboxes at the cross-roads, the intrusions into their houses to fill an attic with sandbags, on to their golf-courses or most fertile fields and gardens to burrow out some wide anti-tank ditch.\" So wrote Winston Churchill in Their Finest Hour, published in 1949."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e532671-c2ed-472a-b0a9-b492c00e96eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "0d6d64b8-fac1-34b2-908b-4c1639fd54e7",
                        "source_sense_id": "d50245d2-6b17-3906-8214-f31e83c59cc4",
                        "target_lang_word": "antichar",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "antichar",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ad62ca5-eb64-35ae-8e06-5cdafcd466e3",
                                        "entry_id": "703ff232-67c0-3435-91dd-7addd178b068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui s’oppose à l’action des blindés, qui nuit aux chars d’assaut."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6546016-a3cf-4a31-9770-cba523e1a6ad",
                                                "sense_id": "5ad62ca5-eb64-35ae-8e06-5cdafcd466e3",
                                                "text": "Il buta contre un fusil antichar anglais enfoui dans le sable. Les dunes étaient jonchées de ces engins. On les reconnaissait de loin à la longueur invraisemblable de leur canon qui s'évasait à l'extrémité comme un tromblon. Cela leur donnait un aspect risible, archaïque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4306258e-b2e5-475c-aa2a-b8e6a5393ed7",
                                                "sense_id": "5ad62ca5-eb64-35ae-8e06-5cdafcd466e3",
                                                "text": "Profitant de la circonstance, le lieutenant-colonel Fumal installa ses canons antichars – préalablement massés derrière le fossé, de Zuydcoote à la mer – entre Zuydcoote et Ghyvelde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "antichar",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d400fd78-1083-33e4-8837-0cbf2366629e",
                                        "entry_id": "4083b8d9-d6b2-3810-b785-46fc324a3bbf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui s’oppose à la multiplication des automobiles par la société."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Québec"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0b211de-1238-4454-9014-154dd0a4f5f5",
                                                "sense_id": "d400fd78-1083-33e4-8837-0cbf2366629e",
                                                "text": "À la pompe à essence, on regarde le prix grimper deux fois plus vite que le nombre de litres qui emplit notre réservoir. Les antichars se réjouissent. Que ces pollueurs d’automobilistes payent !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
